        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: align QA transport and release workflow contracts",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where QA and release operators could follow stale Matrix counts, unsupported live-provider or Telegram flags, incomplete lane selectors, and inaccurate blocking/advisory guidance.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAligns the QA overview, Mantis and release validation docs, and workflow input descriptions with the current private QA CLI and release workflow contracts. Canonical `qa-live-*` selectors are documented while the shipped `qa-matrix` compatibility alias remains accepted.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers can choose the correct Matrix, Telegram, Discord, WhatsApp, and Slack QA lanes, understand their credentials and artifacts, and interpret release failures without stale or inflated guidance.\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex session `019f6784-a4eb-7ce3-af94-d032e0612212`).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx` (731 files)\n- `pnpm docs:check-links` (6,033 internal links; 0 broken)\n- `pnpm format:docs:check` (715 files)\n- Targeted `pnpm format:check` for all six changed files\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/package-acceptance-workflow.test.ts -t 'routes release Matrix|documents the full-release Telegram package path'` (2 passed)\n- Matrix profile resolver: `all=93`, `release=2`, `fast=12`, `transport=50`, `media=7`, `e2ee-smoke=8`, `e2ee-deep=18`, `e2ee-cli=9`\n- Fresh autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe complete workflow test has 72 passing assertions and six pre-existing Telegram-summary harness failures. Those six reproduce with this change's workflow edits removed and are unrelated to this docs/workflow correction.\n",
